y dissertations or submitted work the  entirety of your degree is determined by  a couple of weeks of exams at the end of  Trinity term in your third year well for  the sciences including me I'm a  physicist  things are a little bit different so you  take exams in your second year and your  30th and if you're doing it for your  course up in your fourth year in  addition to any work that forms the  basis of your degree which means that  everything's a bit spread out but it  means you have to do exams over you I am  a fourth year soon I'm a finalist which  means that this set of exams is fingers  crossed the last formal set of exams I'm  ever going  take and I cannot begin to tell you how  happy that makes me  term hasn't actually started here but I  like doing these videos to sort of fill  you in on what's been happening between  the terms and to let you know what's  coming up so first of all next week in  fact I have my college bull understand  Peters college and every other year we  host a black-tie ball this year the  theme is the Roaring Twenties so it's  very jazz based it's gonna be really  really cool  I'm also giving a talk at the  university's computing services about  the role of YouTube in Oxford access and  then of course we've got the exams at  the end of the term but I'm not really  thinking about them too much right now  of course after the exams then we also  have the fun stuff which I am thinking  about right now I do have some quite big  news as the type of the video suggests  actually two bits of news so over the  Easter holidays my channel passed a  thousand subscribers and I really wanted  to say explicitly thank you guys so much  it thought was my mind that anybody  wants to watch these videos frankly so I  truly thank you very much for wanting to  take me I want you to see these videos I  really enjoy making them and from the  feedback I've been going with you guys  it seems like you guys find them useful  so thank you thank you thank you the  